  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Cook potato: Bring a small saucepan of water to the boil for the eggs. Quarter the unpeeled potatoes. Put in a medium saucepan, cover with cold salted water and bring to the boil. Reduce the heat to medium and cook for 10-12 mins until tender. Drain.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1584676/photos/large/122274_1-5a477a58241f87db5583cc29a59b302a.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Boil eggs: Meanwhile, cook 2 eggs in the pan of boiling water for 6 mins for soft-boiled or 8 mins for hard-boiled. Drain, then cool in cold water. Halve the cucumber lengthwise and thickly slice on an angle. Thickly slice the capsicum. Quarter the tofu pieces.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1584677/photos/large/122274_2-c44f57b8936971371fea776d0669ccfe.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make peanut sauce: Combine the coconut milk, peanut butter (see Kitchen notes), 1 tsp curry powder, 2 tsp soy sauce and 1 tsp sugar in the same pan over medium heat. Cook, stirring, for 5-6 mins until slightly thickened. Remove the pan from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1584678/photos/large/122274_3-617738098cbc01cdcd6ceaba234cf972.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Warm tofu: Heat 2 tsp vegetable oil in a medium frypan over medium heat. Cook the tofu for 2 mins each side or until golden and warmed through. Remove from the pan.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1584679/photos/large/122274_4-f286d43b7e2cfc8ca08274f3ac4f2b2a.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Peel and quarter the eggs. Arrange the egg, tofu, potato, cucumber and capsicum on a plate. Spoon over the peanut sauce and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1584680/photos/large/122274_5-46e5e7e30f15152e10bedace59fcceaf.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kitchen notes: Chilli lovers, go wild and scatter over chopped bird's eyes to serve. ~ Peanut butter can firm up upon sitting, so give it a good mix to soften and bring together.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1584681/photos/large/122274_6-a4a9da17c1f79496c57968b72f8dd621.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
